(e.g., presence/dwell/interaction likelihood) and to avoid raw video
retention by default.

Any use intended to bypass, disable, or weaken privacy-preserving behavior
described in the SecuraCV documentation is contrary to the project’s purpose.

Third-party model attribution
-----------------------------
The pinned detection model distributed with SecuraCV releases for the Grove
Vision AI V2 module ("Person Detection", Swift-YOLO 192) originates from the
Seeed Studio SSCMA model zoo and is licensed under the MIT License:
  Copyright (c) 2023 Seeed Technology Co.,Ltd.
  https://github.com/Seeed-Studio/sscma-model-zoo
SecuraCV redistributes it (Vela-compiled for the module's Ethos-U55 NPU)
unmodified in behavior, pinned by SHA-256 to each release
(manifest-vision-model.json).

The Ethos-U55 Vela configuration used to compile it (My_Sys_Cfg /
My_Mem_Mode_Parent, Ethos-U55 64-MAC at 400 MHz) is Himax's own toolchain
config, vendored verbatim in .github/workflows/vision-model-release.yml:
  https://github.com/HimaxWiseEyePlus/ML_FVP_EVALUATION (vela/himax_vela.ini)
